module uim.fiori_blocks.domain.entities;

/// Entities for the domain layer of the application.
/// Domain entities represent the core business objects that have a distinct identity and lifecycle.
/// They encapsulate both data and behavior, ensuring that business rules are consistently enforced.
/// Entities are the primary building blocks of the domain model, and they interact with value objects, domain services, and domain types to implement the business logic.
/// By defining entities with clear boundaries and responsibilities, developers can create a more maintainable and expressive domain model.
/// In essence, domain entities provide a foundation for modeling the key concepts of the business, enabling a robust and adaptable domain layer.
/// They help to ensure that the domain model remains consistent, expressive, and aligned with the business requirements, ultimately leading to higher quality software.
/// This adaptability ensures that the domain layer remains resilient and capable of supporting the evolving needs of the business without compromising the integrity of the domain model.
/// In essence, domain entities provide a foundation for building a flexible, maintainable, and high-quality domain layer that can effectively support the evolving needs of the business.